From 3cd5f0995ee55cb2cf82d23c7d840e38ba36be09 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:24:22 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ga2: built-in SHA-256, launcher program handoff, Windows exec
 quoting

- Disc identity digests use a built-in SHA-256 (x86 SHA extensions when
  available, ~1.7 GB/s; portable otherwise) instead of OpenSSL, so the
  same code builds for Windows (runtime/sha256.h, shared with the launcher).
- LoadExecPS2 under the launcher (GA2_HANDOFF_FILE set) writes the next
  command line to that file and exits with status 75; the launcher runs it
  and keeps waiting. Direct runs still exec. On Windows exec arguments are
  quoted (the CRT joins them unquoted; disc paths contain spaces).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
